.TH INPEDF 1 "November 2026" "inPeDF 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inpedf \- PDF reader for the GNOME desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inpedf
.RI [ FILE ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inpedf
opens PDF documents using GTK 4, Libadwaita and Poppler.
It supports continuous and single-page views, text search and selection,
bookmarks, document outlines, thumbnails, printing and fullscreen presentations.
.PP
Files may be specified as paths or URIs.
When the application is already running, files are sent to the existing instance.
.SH HELP
.B inpedf --help
or
.B inpedf --usage
shows general usage without starting the graphical interface.
Use
.B inpedf export --help
for all batch-export options and examples.
.PP
.B inpedf --version
prints the application version and exits without starting the interface.
.SH EXPORT
.B inpedf export
.RI [ options ] " FILE ..."
.PP
Convert PDFs without starting the graphical interface.
Text is exported page by page; OCR and table reconstruction are not included.
.TP
.BI --format " md,txt,json"
Comma-separated output formats. Default: md.
.TP
.BI --output-dir " DIRECTORY"
Output directory. Default: converted.
.TP
.BI --pages " SELECTION"
Page numbers such as 1,3-5, or all. Default: all.
.TP
.BI --jobs " NUMBER"
Maximum concurrent PDF conversions. Default: 2.
.TP
.B --overwrite
Allow replacing existing output files.
.TP
.BI --password-file " FILE"
Read a shared PDF password from a UTF-8 file.
.TP
.BI --report " FILE"
Write a JSON report with per-file results and failures.
.TP
.B --quiet
Show errors only.
.TP
.B --verbose
Show conversion settings, worker IDs and output paths.
Cannot be combined with --quiet.
.PP
Ctrl+C cancels active conversions and removes incomplete outputs.
Completed files are preserved.
.SH EXIT STATUS
For the export command: 0 indicates success, 1 a conversion or write failure,
2 invalid command options, and 130 cancellation.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a PDF document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Search for text.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Print the document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+0
Set zoom to 100 percent.
.TP
.B F5
Start a presentation from the first page.
.TP
.B Shift+F5
Start a presentation from the current page.
.TP
.B Escape
Leave the presentation or clear the selection.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/inpedf/documents.json
Reading positions and personal bookmarks.
The default state directory is ~/.local/state.
